			<item> <title>Primetime, 2026</title> <link>https://letterboxd.com/mbill/film/primetime-2026/</link> <guid isPermaLink="false">letterboxd-review-1525831014</guid> <pubDate>Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:42:33 +1300</pubDate> <letterboxd:watchedDate>2026-10-05</letterboxd:watchedDate> <letterboxd:rewatch>No</letterboxd:rewatch> <letterboxd:filmTitle>Primetime</letterboxd:filmTitle> <letterboxd:filmYear>2026</letterboxd:filmYear> <letterboxd:memberLike>No</letterboxd:memberLike> <tmdb:movieId>1375441</tmdb:movieId> <description><![CDATA[ <p><img src="https://a.ltrbxd.com/resized/film-poster/1/2/6/2/0/1/9/1262019-primetime-2026-0-600-0-900-crop.jpg?v=41640d6988"/></p> <p>Broke: To Catch A Predator is a manipulative exhibitionist view of the grossest criminals of society<br />Woke: People still do that shit for clicks on Tiktok and Insta, and reality television has gotten three times worse in abusing and exhibiting prisoners and criminals, and no one gives a shit</p><p>This movie pissed me off, it manipulated facts actively disputed in the article it&#039;s based on, it condemns Chris Hansen but is totally okay with the premise of TCAP, and frankly contributes to the same exhibitionist mentality that TCAP pitched and promoted.</p> ]]></description> <dc:creator>MBill</dc:creator> </item>
		
