			<item> <title>Union Town, 2026</title> <link>https://letterboxd.com/mbill/film/union-town/</link> <guid isPermaLink="false">letterboxd-review-1500484543</guid> <pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 01:38:28 +1200</pubDate> <letterboxd:watchedDate>2026-09-18</letterboxd:watchedDate> <letterboxd:rewatch>No</letterboxd:rewatch> <letterboxd:filmTitle>Union Town</letterboxd:filmTitle> <letterboxd:filmYear>2026</letterboxd:filmYear> <letterboxd:memberLike>No</letterboxd:memberLike> <tmdb:movieId>1736513</tmdb:movieId> <description><![CDATA[ <p><img src="https://a.ltrbxd.com/resized/film-poster/1/6/0/2/6/3/4/1602634-union-town-0-600-0-900-crop.jpg?v=c256d671a5"/></p> <p>A good doc, but not necessarily to the same heights of intimacy or intrigue of Kopple&#039;s other labour documentaries. Ultimately, I&#039;m okay with that though, given that there&#039;s a whole lot more wins and positivity in the modern world than <i>Harlan County</i>, and certainly <i>American Dream</i>. Not to say there aren&#039;t many problems still to be fixed, but things have certainly improved since the 80s. It&#039;s telling how little any faces of the corporations are actually shown outside of secondary footage, the playbook has become very cold and cruel.</p> ]]></description> <dc:creator>MBill</dc:creator> </item>
		
			<item> <title>Ladies and Gentlemen, Brian Mulroney, 2026</title> <link>https://letterboxd.com/mbill/film/ladies-and-gentlemen-brian-mulroney/</link> <guid isPermaLink="false">letterboxd-review-1498031873</guid> <pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 18:36:16 +1200</pubDate> <letterboxd:watchedDate>2026-09-16</letterboxd:watchedDate> <letterboxd:rewatch>No</letterboxd:rewatch> <letterboxd:filmTitle>Ladies and Gentlemen, Brian Mulroney</letterboxd:filmTitle> <letterboxd:filmYear>2026</letterboxd:filmYear> <letterboxd:memberLike>Yes</letterboxd:memberLike> <tmdb:movieId>1727146</tmdb:movieId> <description><![CDATA[ <p><img src="https://a.ltrbxd.com/resized/film-poster/1/5/9/3/9/0/7/1593907-ladies-and-gentlemen-brian-mulroney-0-600-0-900-crop.jpg?v=3a4ebaf2a5"/></p> <p>EXCELLENT. Fabulous infotainment, so much fun. So glad I made it out for this one. I&#039;m so glad there&#039;s this weird side to Canadian film, and I&#039;m glad that the NFB was the one able to help enable it. Never a waste of tax payer money. And remember, Mulroney doesn&#039;t play footsie.</p> ]]></description> <dc:creator>MBill</dc:creator> </item>
		
